WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.010 --> 00:00:05.390
Hey youtubers it's Charlie and this week we
got two new episodes of Korra. This video

00:00:05.390 --> 00:00:10.180
is going to be my combined review of both
of them, episodes 4 and 5. Episode 4 was the

00:00:10.180 --> 00:00:16.150
conclusion of a two parter and Episode 5 was
the beginning of another two parter, so technically

00:00:16.150 --> 00:00:19.590
they weren't paired up correctly but I'll
explain.

00:00:19.590 --> 00:00:22.810
Hello new people, if you're just finding me
for the first time I'm doing weekly Korra

00:00:22.810 --> 00:00:26.400
videos. Be sure to subscribe to get everything.
Quick shoutout to the winner of last week's

00:00:26.400 --> 00:00:32.870
giveaway The Real Spider Mew. You win an amazon
gift card. All you have to do to enter the

00:00:32.870 --> 00:00:35.219
giveaway is be a subscriber and leave a comment.

00:00:35.219 --> 00:00:37.579
Because there's two episodes for this video
I'll be picking two people randomly. I'll

00:00:37.579 --> 00:00:39.429
let you know who wins in next week's video.

00:00:39.429 --> 00:00:44.479
So I'm going to start with my top 10 moments
from both episodes, then do my review. Careful

00:00:44.479 --> 00:00:51.049
for spoilers if you haven't seen the episodes
yet. I'll wait just a sec...Here we go Number

00:00:51.049 --> 00:00:54.670
10 - Welcome to Zaofu, City of the Metalbenders

00:00:54.670 --> 00:00:59.010
This is an Avatar first, we've never seen
a city made completely of metal before. It's

00:00:59.010 --> 00:01:02.769
like looking at a metal garden. My favorite
part of it was the Dance Academy with the

00:01:02.769 --> 00:01:04.869
Metal Flower they were using to practice with.

00:01:04.869 --> 00:01:11.869
In the trailers I actually thought we were
seeing them practice fighting. Which is funny

00:01:11.880 --> 00:01:16.220
because it's a nice mirror for the story in
Episode 4 with the Dai Li Airbending army

00:01:16.220 --> 00:01:23.220
training and what will turn into the Northern
Air Temple training in episode 6.

00:01:28.450 --> 00:01:33.450
Couple important facts about it. Suyin built
it with the help of her husband, and Toph

00:01:33.450 --> 00:01:38.740
just visited it. As Opal described meeting
Grandma Toph.

00:01:38.740 --> 00:01:42.780
When she called it the safest city in the
world she was probably referring to the metal

00:01:42.780 --> 00:01:47.130
rose petals covering the buildings at night.
Since those were so large I'm going to assume

00:01:47.130 --> 00:01:51.150
it takes several metalbenders working together
to open and close them.

00:01:51.150 --> 00:01:56.260
It seems like a city of artists and reformed
criminals looking for a new way of life. Which

00:01:56.260 --> 00:02:00.100
kind of explains why Suyin thought the idea
of the Earth Kingdom still having a Queen

00:02:00.100 --> 00:02:01.440
was ridiculous.

00:02:01.440 --> 00:02:04.540
Who else is hoping that we get to see a classic
Fire Ferrets scene with that Metal Bending

00:02:04.540 --> 00:02:06.960
game. It looked almost like a combination
of billiards and foozeball.

00:02:06.960 --> 00:02:09.929
9 - New Characters Opal and Suyin Beifong

00:02:09.929 --> 00:02:13.680
So there were actually a lot of new characters
and Suyin has five children not just Opal.

00:02:13.680 --> 00:02:19.489
But Opal and Suyin are the big ones. All the
Bolin shipping makes it pretty clear Opal

00:02:19.489 --> 00:02:25.469
will eventually join team korra and help them.
Opal is voiced by Alyson Stoner and Suyin

00:02:25.469 --> 00:02:28.959
is voiced by Anne Heche.

00:02:28.959 --> 00:02:33.549
This episode was just the first part of a
two part episode, so next week we'll get a

00:02:33.549 --> 00:02:37.700
nice Beifong flashback with Toph in it that
will explain why Lin hates her sister so much.

00:02:37.700 --> 00:02:41.739
She came off like a bitch, but really we don't
know what her beef is, so don't be too quick

00:02:41.739 --> 00:02:46.849
to judge. They said it had been 30 years,
so whatever Suyin did that Lin claims broke

00:02:46.849 --> 00:02:49.209
their family apart, I'm hoping they show it.

00:02:49.209 --> 00:02:54.700
I know they'll show how she got her scars
on her face, they showed them off quite a

00:02:54.700 --> 00:03:00.779
bit in episode 5, but I find it hard to believe
that was the event that tore their family

00:03:00.779 --> 00:03:05.760
apart for 30 years.

00:03:05.760 --> 00:03:10.909
Since Tenzin's family became a huge part of
book 2, I'm wondering if Suyin also follows

00:03:10.909 --> 00:03:14.819
Team Korra around this season. It sounds like
they will eventually resolve their Beifong

00:03:14.819 --> 00:03:19.810
family issues so I'm expecting a similar team
up in the finale just like we got with Aang's

00:03:19.810 --> 00:03:21.349
children.

00:03:21.349 --> 00:03:25.189
Really the most interesting thing from their
interaction was when Suyin explained that

00:03:25.189 --> 00:03:29.309
neither of them knew their fathers. If you
didn't catch it, they're only half sisters.

00:03:29.309 --> 00:03:33.379
I'm betting that The Duke was one of their
fathers and the other one was a character

00:03:33.379 --> 00:03:34.760
we haven't met yet.

00:03:34.760 --> 00:03:41.659
If Sokka were Lin's father it would make things
really awkward since Lin and Tenzin were lovers

00:03:41.659 --> 00:03:46.189
when they were children. I don't think they'll
reveal who the fathers were until Book 4 or

00:03:46.189 --> 00:03:53.029
until Toph returns, if she ever does. But
they could also use the comics to reveal who

00:03:53.029 --> 00:03:53.659
they are.

00:03:53.659 --> 00:03:56.169
Number 8 - Team Korra Prison Break

00:03:56.169 --> 00:04:00.309
Lots of Prison Breaks going on in the episode,
both very cool. I'm interested to see what

00:04:00.309 --> 00:04:05.309
the consequences of Korra's actions are or
if they just drop the plot. The Earth Queen

00:04:05.309 --> 00:04:08.620
claims that taking the airbenders was an act
of war, but unless the Earth Queen mobilizes

00:04:08.620 --> 00:04:14.040
against the Northern Air Temple, I don't think
anything is going to happen.

00:04:14.040 --> 00:04:17.579
We got to see Jinora use her new ability.
It seems kind of like a cross between energy

00:04:17.579 --> 00:04:21.500
bending and entering the spirit world. Like
she's separating her consciousness from her

00:04:21.500 --> 00:04:26.940
body, but is still able to remain in the physical
realm.

00:04:26.940 --> 00:04:33.940
Even though the Spirits are roaming free,
the spirit realm is still a separate domain

00:04:34.450 --> 00:04:41.270
from the physical realm. You can still travel
there.

00:04:41.270 --> 00:04:45.170
Number 7 - Team Zahir Breaks out Sparky Sparky
Boom Girl

00:04:45.170 --> 00:04:50.010
As cool as this was, all I could think about
was the similiarities between Team Zahir and

00:04:50.010 --> 00:04:53.660
Team Korra. They seemed like totally sane
normal people just trying to get their friend

00:04:53.660 --> 00:05:00.550
out. They had sense's of humor, they made
jokes and had regular emotions.

00:05:00.550 --> 00:05:05.300
This is in contrast to previous villains like
Amon and Unalaq that were pretty much straight

00:05:05.300 --> 00:05:10.570
up black hat wearing villains. There was almost
no doubt they were bad.

00:05:10.570 --> 00:05:14.160
The way they're developing Team Zahir makes
me wonder if they're going to end up helping

00:05:14.160 --> 00:05:19.570
Korra do something important. Like bring about
a new age that is good, but only seems bad

00:05:19.570 --> 00:05:26.570
because Tenzin, Sokka and Zuko never found
out what their plan was.

00:05:27.500 --> 00:05:30.030
Number 6 - Dai Li Training Camp

00:05:30.030 --> 00:05:34.420
Did anybody else think of Karate Kid whenever
the Dai Li was yelling no mercy. All I could

00:05:34.420 --> 00:05:37.520
think was no mercy in our dojo.

00:05:37.520 --> 00:05:43.670
What's really amazed me about all the new
airbenders is how good some of them are despite

00:05:43.670 --> 00:05:48.350
not having any training. Zahir is the most
extreme example of that. Like he seems like

00:05:48.350 --> 00:05:53.100
he's been bending for years. And Kai even
seems really sophisticated with his technique.

00:05:53.100 --> 00:05:56.350
Especially when he saved Jinora from the Dai
Li.

00:05:56.350 --> 00:06:01.960
I don't expect them to explain why, I think
we're just supposed to take away that they're

00:06:01.960 --> 00:06:05.690
naturally gifted like Azula or Aang.

00:06:05.690 --> 00:06:08.050
Number 5 - Varrick Returns

00:06:08.050 --> 00:06:15.050
Now he's supposedly building a Maglev high
speed rail system. I loved that they kind

00:06:15.180 --> 00:06:19.030
of buried the lead here and made it seem like
he was doing weird spiritual things with magnets.

00:06:19.030 --> 00:06:23.990
Even though Varrick is a qualified douchebag,
he does actually conduct normal business.

00:06:23.990 --> 00:06:28.070
So high speed rail seems in keeping with the
series take on modernization.

00:06:28.070 --> 00:06:33.760
It's like we go from feudalism in Aang's time,
to cars and mechs in Korra's time. High Speed

00:06:33.760 --> 00:06:36.330
rail is just the next step.
After that it's not too long before you see

00:06:36.330 --> 00:06:38.980
microchips and energy based weapons.

00:06:38.980 --> 00:06:40.780
Number 4 - All of the new Ships

00:06:40.780 --> 00:06:45.310
When Mike and Bryan said that teenage romance
wouldn't be as big of a thing this season

00:06:45.310 --> 00:06:50.700
I didn't really know what it meant. Because
of Jikya and Bopal now, I'm thinking yes there

00:06:50.700 --> 00:06:54.300
will be romance, the story just won't feature
it on screen as much.

00:06:54.300 --> 00:06:57.990
So for instance, Korra interrupting Bolin
and Opal is probably just a way for them to

00:06:57.990 --> 00:07:02.020
tell us, yes they'll probably be doing stuff
whenever they're off by themselves. When we

00:07:02.020 --> 00:07:05.850
see them on screen with everyone else, they
probably won't go crazy with boyfriend girlfriend

00:07:05.850 --> 00:07:06.080
moments.

00:07:06.080 --> 00:07:08.470
Number 3 - Kya vs Zahir

00:07:08.470 --> 00:07:12.670
It's awesome that Kya doesn't have to just
be the healer this season. When we met her

00:07:12.670 --> 00:07:17.130
last year she seemed like more of a hippie.
I'm glad we get to see more female characters

00:07:17.130 --> 00:07:19.730
on the show that aren't just mothers or healers.

00:07:19.730 --> 00:07:24.100
You can totally be a badass waterbender or
a cranky pants metalbender.

00:07:24.100 --> 00:07:28.480
More to that, even on Team Zahir, it's the
female members that have thus far seemed like

00:07:28.480 --> 00:07:34.450
the most proficient. The armless waterbender
Ming Hua and Pi Li the sparky sparky boom

00:07:34.450 --> 00:07:35.510
girl.

00:07:35.510 --> 00:07:38.800
Number 2 - Lin and Tenzin Explain Team Zaheer

00:07:38.800 --> 00:07:43.680
The biggest WTF from all of this is that they
still have no idea why Zaheer wanted to kidnap

00:07:43.680 --> 00:07:47.910
the avatar. Clearly it's going to be the red
herring this season, but Harmonic Convergence

00:07:47.910 --> 00:07:52.700
has already happened and Korra has already
been separated from Raava, who was killed,

00:07:52.700 --> 00:07:57.880
then resurrected to reform the Avatar. So
what could Zaheer possibly want to do that

00:07:57.880 --> 00:07:59.389
would top that?

00:07:59.389 --> 00:08:02.910
They don't seem evil, so I don't think they
wanted to kill her.

00:08:02.910 --> 00:08:06.750
I'm wondering if they're going to hold of
explaining their plan until the last couple

00:08:06.750 --> 00:08:11.410
of episodes. It didn't really become clear
what the Unalaq Vaatu plan was till after

00:08:11.410 --> 00:08:13.420
the Avatar Wan episodes last year.

00:08:13.420 --> 00:08:20.260
and my Number 1 moment wasn't any of the big
shocking reveals, it was Zahir reading Tenzin's

00:08:20.260 --> 00:08:22.460
pendant. The one that belonged to Guru Lahima.

00:08:22.460 --> 00:08:28.970
Here's what it said "Let go of your earthly
attachments, enter the void and become the

00:08:28.970 --> 00:08:30.020
wind".

00:08:30.020 --> 00:08:36.479
Everytime we get a long Zaheer scene we learn
a little more about what he's thinking about.

00:08:36.479 --> 00:08:42.960
I interpreted the poem as one, being the guiding
principle of airbenders. Leaving behind earthly

00:08:42.960 --> 00:08:46.010
attachments and pursuing a more spiritual
life.

00:08:46.010 --> 00:08:49.820
But it's the part about entering the void
that got me thinking. I'm wondering if Zaheer

00:08:49.820 --> 00:08:52.730
wants to use Korra to master death.

00:08:52.730 --> 00:08:58.010
That's just my first take, I might think about
it differently in a couple weeks. But let

00:08:58.010 --> 00:09:02.950
me know what you think the poem meant in that
context. When Zaheer said it.

00:09:02.950 --> 00:09:07.050
I didn't mention it before, but Ikki teaching
the airbenders how to use the airbending gates

00:09:07.050 --> 00:09:13.279
was so funny. As creepy as Zaheer was, I loved
that he bowed to Ikki after he used them.

00:09:13.279 --> 00:09:19.130
I secretly wonder if everything he says has
a double meaning. He said each student is

00:09:19.130 --> 00:09:23.130
only as good as their master, so does that
mean he studied under an airbending master

00:09:23.130 --> 00:09:24.820
at some point or a guru?

00:09:24.820 --> 00:09:30.029
He seems like he knows more about bending
history and lore than Unalaq did.

00:09:30.029 --> 00:09:33.830
Let me know what your favorite moment was,
I'm going to say Team Zaheer was awesome,

00:09:33.830 --> 00:09:38.350
I can't wait to see more of their scenes.
Ikki being the leaf was hilarious and I loved

00:09:38.350 --> 00:09:40.660
the metal bending city.

00:09:40.660 --> 00:09:45.330
Overall this was probably my favorite episode
this season so far. I gave it an A just for

00:09:45.330 --> 00:09:48.800
character development and for the way it dealt
with female relationships without getting

00:09:48.800 --> 00:09:53.420
to catty like you see on a lot of children's
shows. The Lin Beifong pathos is so rich with

00:09:53.420 --> 00:09:56.900
untold backstory. I can't wait for some flashbacks.

00:09:56.900 --> 00:10:01.650
The setup they're doing for Zaheer's mystery
plan seems so big, I have to believe it has

00:10:01.650 --> 00:10:08.650
something to do with conquering death. And
the music was so much fun. The tracks during

00:10:10.140 --> 00:10:14.370
the prison break and the old timey music during
the dinner scene were my favorite songs.

00:10:14.370 --> 00:10:19.310
They usually wait forever to release soundtracks,
so I might have to try to extract them from

00:10:19.310 --> 00:10:22.540
a broadcast or something until they release
them on itunes.

00:10:22.540 --> 00:10:27.120
Next week's episode is the second part of
the earth kingdom story. They only thing I

00:10:27.120 --> 00:10:33.560
don't like about what's going on right now
is the way Nickelodeon is mismatching episodes.

00:10:33.560 --> 00:10:39.000
Forget doubling up, if they're going to do
that I can live with it, but at least pair

00:10:39.000 --> 00:10:41.940
two parters with the right story arcs.

00:10:41.940 --> 00:10:46.040
Because this is my combined episode 4 5 review,
I'll be doing a Q&amp;A tomorrow, so be sure to

00:10:46.040 --> 00:10:50.990
subscribe to get it. I'll announce the giveaway
winners. Normally I'd wait till next week.

00:10:50.990 --> 00:10:55.120
Right now click here to get that, I'll add
the annotation as soon as I post it. And click

00:10:55.120 --> 00:10:58.110
here for my top 10 last airbender characters
on Korra.

00:10:58.110 --> 00:11:00.520
Thanks for watching, see you guys tomorrow.
High Fives!

